%% 10_lld/02_systems_lld/04_lockfree_data_structures - epoch-based reclamation: why a retired object is safe to free
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Control thread
  participant E as Epoch manager
  participant R1 as Reader 1
  participant R2 as Reader 2

  Note over E: global epoch = N

  R1->>E: enter() - pins epoch N
  C->>C: build new rule table
  C->>C: publish pointer (release store)
  C->>E: retire(old table) into limbo[N]
  C->>E: try_advance()
  E-->>C: blocked - R1 still pinned at N

  R1->>E: exit()
  R2->>E: enter() - pins epoch N
  C->>E: try_advance()
  E->>E: all pinned readers at N, advance to N+1
  Note over E: anything retired in limbo[N-1] is now unreachable
  E->>E: free limbo[N-1]

  Note over R1,R2: readers never blocked, never took a lock
